WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.010
Switch on an ordinary filament
lamp and spread its light out.

2
00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.070
You get a smooth, unbroken rainbow.

3
00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:10.210
Now do the same with the
light from a neon sign.

4
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:11.760
No rainbow this time.

5
00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:15.710
Just a few sharp, bright
lines on a dark background.

6
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:17.850
Where did the rest of the rainbow go?

7
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.200
Why only these few lines?

8
00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.310
In this mission, you'll meet
three kinds of spectrum,

9
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:25.710
and the sources that make each one.

10
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.140
Then you'll read spectra
like fingerprints,

11
00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:32.650
the way helium was discovered
in the Sun's light in 1868.

12
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:38.020
Your mission: explain why a neon sign
glows in a few sharp lines instead of a

13
00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.160
full rainbow.
